From 93edf65f1e3f798cd4c677b0ec6571a24c2e019c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 20:31:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07147/11362] [outer-loop] exp5705 v2: timeout-margin retry
 killed by outer wrapper, zero output (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5599-2)

Operator asked whether v1's proposer_failed verdict was a timeout artifact
rather than genuine model-quality failure. Real prefill measurement (via
llama_cpp vocab_only tokenize + n_predict=1) confirmed the timeout margin
was genuinely tight (worst case ~1270s vs v1's timeout=1200). A retry with
timeout=3600 (3x margin) wrapped in a 7200s outer budget was killed with
zero output after 2 hours of continuous, genuine GPU compute (rocm-smi
100% util, llama-server R state, climbing RSS/CPU-time throughout -- not a
hang). This falsifies the "just needed more time" hypothesis and closes
the question: the candidate cannot complete the live reinduction task in
a bounded window on this hardware at Q8_0, independent of timeout chosen.
v1 artifact remains the checked-in measurement (retry produced nothing to
overwrite it with); no third retry launched without operator check-in.
